From: Thomas Petazzoni <thomas.petazzoni@free-electrons.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: use pkg-config to discover libusb

This allows to remove hardcoded paths to libusb headers.

[Regenerated for hplip 3.26.6 by PengyOS, 2026-10-19. Buildroot's original
 (1eed2b65eff4, carried at package/hplip/0001-...patch) targets Makefile.am
 line 92; the hardcoded -I/usr/include/libusb-1.0 is at line 125 in 3.26.6 with
 different surrounding lines, so the original hunk fails outright
 ("Hunk #1 FAILED at 92"). Same change, the 3.26.6 context.

 Both hunks are needed, and that is worth stating because dropping the
 configure.in half looks harmless and is not: Makefile.am references
 $(LIBUSB_CFLAGS)/$(LIBUSB_LIBS), and automake only emits those assignments
 when configure AC_SUBSTs them, which is PKG_CHECK_MODULES that does it. With
 the configure.in hunk dropped the variables expand to nothing, the -I for
 libusb is lost, and the build dies with
   io/hpmud/musb.h:33:10: fatal error: libusb.h: No such file or directory
 Carried on our own recipe (divergence.toml -> hplip-3.26.6-fork).]

Signed-off-by: Thomas Petazzoni <thomas.petazzoni@free-electrons.com>
---
 Makefile.am  | 4 ++--
 configure.in | 3 +--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -122,8 +122,8 @@
 libhpmud_la_LDFLAGS += -lusb
 else
 libhpmud_la_SOURCES += io/hpmud/musb.c 
-libhpmud_la_CFLAGS  += -I/usr/include/libusb-1.0
-libhpmud_la_LDFLAGS += -lusb-1.0
+libhpmud_la_CFLAGS  += $(LIBUSB_CFLAGS)
+libhpmud_la_LDFLAGS += $(LIBUSB_LIBS)
 endif
 
 
diff --git a/configure.in b/configure.in
--- a/configure.in
+++ b/configure.in
@@ -617,8 +617,7 @@
       AC_CHECK_LIB([usb], [usb_init], [LIBS="$LIBS"], [AC_MSG_ERROR([cannot find libusb support], 2)])
       AC_CHECK_HEADERS(usb.h, ,[AC_MSG_ERROR([cannot find libusb-devel support], 11)])
    else
-      AC_CHECK_LIB([usb-1.0], [libusb_init], [LIBS="$LIBS"], [AC_MSG_ERROR([cannot find libusb 1.0 support], 2)])
-      AC_CHECK_HEADERS(libusb-1.0/libusb.h, ,[AC_MSG_ERROR([cannot find libusb-1.0-devel support], 11)])
+      PKG_CHECK_MODULES([LIBUSB], [libusb-1.0])
    fi
 fi
 
